#SAE steel grades
Carbon steel: 4 digits, 3+4 digits carbon content
- 1xxx: carbon
- 2xxx: nickel
- 3xxx: nickel-chromium
- 4xxx: molybdenum
- 5xxx: chromium
- 6xxx: chromium-vanadium
- 7xxx: tungsten
- 8xxx: nickel-chromium-molybdenum
- 9xxx: silicon-manganese
Stainless steel: 3 digits
- 3xx: chromium-nickel
- 304: most common, 18% Cr + 8% Ni
- 316: marine environment, molybdenum
- 4xx: chromium
- 420: cutlery
- 440: higher-grade cutlery

=fabric weave
Weft: horizontal thread
Warp: vertical thread
Satin weave: smooth and lustrous, warps go over many wefts then under one
Plain weave: strong, warps go over one weft then under one, crossing pattern
Twill weave: warps go over several wefts then under several, diagonal pattern
